<title>GERMANY: DG Bank H1 gp oper profit after provs up 30.1 pct. [CORRECTED 9:21 GMT]</title>
<headline>DG Bank H1 gp oper profit after provs up 30.1 pct. [CORRECTED 9:21 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group oper profit after provisions    266.2  vs 204.6</p>
<p>    Group net bad debt provisions	   188.1  vs 213.4</p>
<p>    Gp net own-account trading income	80.3  vs  91.3</p>
<p>    Gp administrative expenses	    1,351.6  vs 1,233.7</p>
<p>    Group personnel costs		     663.7  vs 616.2</p>
<p>    Group net commission income	     138.5  vs 143.9</p>
<p>    Group net interest income	     1,598.7  vs 1,385.7</p>
<p>    Group partial operating profit	  385.6  vs   295.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German bank is DG Bank AG. The comparative figures for H1 1995 represent 50 percent of figures for the full year, not actual H1 results. The bank said its parent group operating profit after provisions rose to 226.8 million marks from 174.8 million marks in H1 1995.</p>
<p>(Corrects to make clear H1 1995 figure refers to parent earnings, not group earnings).</p>
</text>
